  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "The 2026 election for Ohio's 5th Congressional District pits 10-term Republican incumbent Bob Latta against Democratic nominee Brian Shaver and independent candidate Dalton Franklin. The district, which stretches from Lorain County to the Indiana border, includes Elyria, Findlay, Norwalk, Bowling Green, and Van Wert. Redistricting in October 2025 adjusted the map for the 2026 cycle, but the Cook Political Report continues to rate the district as Solidly Republican. Latta, a senior member of the House Energy and Commerce Committee and chair of the Energy Subcommittee, faces his first Democratic challenger since the district was redrawn, while Shaver campaigned on congressional accountability and campaign finance reform.",
