      "name": "Bob Latta",
      "party": "Republican Party",
      "incumbent": true,
      "summary": "Bob Latta is the 10-term incumbent U.S. Representative for Ohio's 5th Congressional District, first elected in a December 2007 special election following the death of Rep. Paul Gillmor. He serves as a senior member of the House Energy and Commerce Committee, where he chairs the Subcommittee on Energy, and has authored legislation on the opioid crisis, drinking water safety, and nuclear energy. Latta previously served in the Ohio House of Representatives, the Ohio Senate, and as a Wood County Commissioner.",
